--- !u!114 &8328270483791888212
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2572244962536692934}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "He was just a man.\nA little pale. A little reclusive. Lived alone in
    a dim little apartment not far from Jerry\u2019s.\nHe paid his bills.\nHe minded
    his own.\nAnd he kept his phone locked \u2014 ten characters, uppercase, symbols,
    the whole checklist.\nHe did everything right.\n\nUntil the quiz.\n\nIt looked
    legitimate.\nSomething about mobile security awareness.\n\"Free gift card if
    you complete the assessment.\"\nHe thought, why not?\nHe typed it all in \u2014
    habits, settings, even his backup phrase.\n\nAnd that was it.\n\nWithin hours,
    his phone was hijacked.\nHis accounts drained.\nHis name used in things he couldn\u2019t
    take back.\nThey knew everything.\nNot just passwords.\nNot just contacts.\nHim.\n\nHe
    went to the police. They shrugged.\nHe changed his passwords. It was too late.\nHe
    tried to warn others. No one listened.\nHe became a ghost in his own home.\nStopped
    sleeping.\nStopped eating.\nThen... stopped existing.\n\nNow, what\u2019s left
    is something else.\nThe Freak.\n\nPale. Crooked. Hollow-eyed.\nTwisted by regret
    and static.\nHe lives inside the walls of devices now, lurking between login
    screens and signal noise.\nHe is the ghost of a data breach made flesh \u2014
    an embodiment of caution, corrupted by trauma and failure.\nHe doesn\u2019t want
    revenge.\nHe wants prevention.\n\nBecause if he can stop one more soul from clicking
    \u201CAccept,\u201D\nFrom giving away what can\u2019t be returned\u2014\nHe isn\u2019t
    malicious. He\u2019s desperate.\n\nThat\u2019s why he\u2019s here now.\nIn Jerry\u2019s
    apartment.\nWatching as the old man hovers his mouse over that same quiz.\nThe
    one that ended his life."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
